@startuml
!include ../shortfall/style.iuml
title Parsing and executing list-recipes 2
autonumber

participant "MishMash" as App
participant "parser: Parser" as Parser
participant "list: ListRecipeCommand" as List
participant "book: RecipeBook" as Book
participant "viewer: RecipeViewer" as Viewer

App -> Parser : parseCommand("list-recipes 2")
activate Parser
note right of Parser : Dispatch to parseListRecipe is condensed.
Parser -> Parser : parseRecipeIndex("2")
note right of Parser
  Accepts digits only, within the int range, and at least 1.
  Anything else throws IllegalArgumentException, which
  parseListRecipe wraps in a MishMashException that ends
  with the list-recipes format.
end note
create List
Parser -> List : new ListRecipeCommand(2)
Parser --> App : list
deactivate Parser

note over App, List : confirmationPrompt(book) returns an empty Optional, so no question is asked.
App -> List : execute(book)
activate List
List -> Book : getRecipes()
Book --> List : recipes (read-only copy)
alt recipes is empty, or index exceeds recipes.size()
  List --> App : throws MishMashException
  note over App, List : The caller displays the error followed by all command formats.
else index is valid
  create Viewer
  List -> Viewer : new RecipeViewer()
  List -> Viewer : view(recipes.get(index - 1))
  Viewer --> List : name, nutrition, ingredients, food tags
  List --> App : details of recipe 2
end
deactivate List

note over App, Viewer
  Without an index, parseListRecipe creates ListRecipeCommand() and execute builds the
  numbered list itself ("Recipes:" plus one line per recipe, or "No recipes yet...").
  No viewer is used and an empty book is not an error. Neither path changes the book.
end note
@enduml
